  "text_input": "Patient is a 42-year-old female, known case of T-cell lymphoblastic leukemia on chemotherapy (Doxorubicin, Vincristine, Methotrexate), presenting with bilateral lower limb swelling for 5 days and breathlessness for 1 day. Vitals on admission showed SpO2 of 86% on room air, BP 130/62 mmHg, and pulse 86 bpm. CT pulmonary angiography (CTPA) revealed chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD), pulmonary arterial hypertension (PAH), and mediastinal/axillary lymphadenopathy. Laboratory findings were significant for anemia of chronic disease. The patient was managed with antibiotics (Inj Rifco), nebulization, and analgesics, and referred for specialized oncological management.",
